  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "If the dollar ever lost its reserve-currency crown, here's the chain of what it would actually do to your money.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "globe",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "If the dollar",
            "lost the crown."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "First, the world needs fewer dollars. Then demand drops. Then imports cost more. Then inflation bites, and borrowing gets dearer.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "The consequence chain",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "Less demand",
              "value": "→",
              "note": "world holds fewer dollars",
              "color": "#5c544c",
              "bar": 0.3
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "Dollar falls",
              "value": "→",
              "note": "imports cost more",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.55
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "Inflation",
              "value": "↑",
              "note": "your money buys less",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.8
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "Rates rise",
              "value": "↑",
              "note": "debt gets dearer",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A reserve currency is one other nations hold and trade in by default.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-reserve",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · reserve currency"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That global demand is exactly what lets America import cheaply and borrow for less.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "the perk",
          "label": "cheap imports, cheap debt",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Economists call that perk America's exorbitant privilege.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-exorbitant",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · exorbitant privilege"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Strip it away, and everyday prices and interest rates would likely grind higher.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Prices grind up",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A weaker currency feeds straight into higher inflation.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-inflation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · inflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And once that kind of spiral gets going, it tends to quietly feed on itself.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "It feeds itself",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That is exactly why any talk of de-dollarisation makes policymakers so nervous.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-dedollar",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · de-dollarisation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So out of that whole chain, which step worries you the most?",
